<title>Tinnitus: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0118-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Tinnitus. Perform history and physical, and audiometry. Subjective or objective? tinnitus?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Subjective</path>
<path target="cell-3">Objective</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Unilateral tinnitus, bilateral tinnitus, or trauma?</label>
<path target="cell-4">Unilateral</path>
<path target="cell-5">Trauma</path>
<path target="cell-6">Bilateral</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Abnormal ear examination?</label>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Order MRI.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Consider cerumen impaction or infection.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Treat as appropriate.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Hearing loss?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Consider otosclerosis, presbycusis, ototoxicity.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Consider metabolic causes, psychogenic tinnitus, ototoxicity.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Pulsatile tinnitus?</label>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
<path target="cell-12">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Consider palatal myoclonus, stapedial muscle spasm, patulous Eustachian tube. Order MRI.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Consider vascular etiology - order CT&#x002F;MRA</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>From Collins RD. Algorithmic Diagnosis of Symptoms and Signs: A Cost-effective Approach. 2d ed. Philadelphia: Lippincott Williams and Wilkins, 2003: 568-569.<xref ref="book1" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
